    "statementHTML": "<div class=\"statement-body\">\n<div class=\"statement-section statement-goal\">\n   <h2><span class=\"icon icon-goal\">&nbsp;</span><span>Goal </span></h2>\n   <span class=\"question-statement\">The Japanese abacus (soroban) is a calculation tool that uses vertical columns (<const>|</const>) of beads to represent a floating-point number. Each column has <const>1</const> bead on the top and <const>4</const> beads at the bottom; the position of the beads denotes a <strong>corresponding place (digit) value</strong> of the resultant number.<br><br>The abacus, with all columns set to value <const>0</const>, looks like this in ASCII:<br><pre style=\"font-family: monospace\"></pre><pre style=\"font-family: monospace\"> _________________________________________________________ <br>/  _____________________________________________________  \\<br>| | &lt;_&gt; &lt;_&gt; &lt;_&gt; &lt;_&gt; &lt;_&gt; &lt;_&gt; &lt;_&gt; &lt;_&gt; &lt;_&gt; &lt;_&gt; &lt;_&gt; &lt;_&gt; &lt;_&gt; | |<br>| |__|___|___|___|___|___|___|___|___|___|___|___|___|__| |<br>|  __________________________.__________________________  |<br>| |  |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |  | |<br>| | &lt;_&gt; &lt;_&gt; &lt;_&gt; &lt;_&gt; &lt;_&gt; &lt;_&gt; &lt;_&gt; &lt;_&gt; &lt;_&gt; &lt;_&gt; &lt;_&gt; &lt;_&gt; &lt;_&gt; | |<br>| | &lt;_&gt; &lt;_&gt; &lt;_&gt; &lt;_&gt; &lt;_&gt; &lt;_&gt; &lt;_&gt; &lt;_&gt; &lt;_&gt; &lt;_&gt; &lt;_&gt; &lt;_&gt; &lt;_&gt; | |<br>| | &lt;_&gt; &lt;_&gt; &lt;_&gt; &lt;_&gt; &lt;_&gt; &lt;_&gt; &lt;_&gt; &lt;_&gt; &lt;_&gt; &lt;_&gt; &lt;_&gt; &lt;_&gt; &lt;_&gt; | |<br>| |_&lt;_&gt;_&lt;_&gt;_&lt;_&gt;_&lt;_&gt;_&lt;_&gt;_&lt;_&gt;_&lt;_&gt;_&lt;_&gt;_&lt;_&gt;_&lt;_&gt;_&lt;_&gt;_&lt;_&gt;_&lt;_&gt;_| |<br>\\_________________________________________________________/</pre><pre style=\"font-family: monospace\"></pre><br>To read the number displayed on the abacus, follow these steps in order:<br><br>1. Find the <strong>dot</strong> (<const>.</const>) located on the middle row of the abacus frame. The column indicated by the dot denotes the <strong>ones digit place</strong> - all columns to the left of and including the dotted column represent the <strong>integer value</strong> of the number, while all columns to the right of (and excluding) the dotted column represent the <strong>decimal value</strong> of the number.<br><br>2. Determine each place value from the bead positions in each column. If the top bead is shifted down towards the middle row of the abacus frame, that bead adds <const>5</const> to the total place value. For each bottom bead shifted up towards the middle row of the abacus frame, that bead adds <const>1</const> to the total place value.<br><br>3. String all place values together (accounting for the decimal point) and truncate unnecessary leading and/or trailing zeroes and/or the radix character (<const>.</const>) to obtain the final value of the represented number.<br><br>For example, the following ASCII abacus represents the number <const>12345.6789</const>:<br><pre style=\"font-family: monospace\"></pre><pre style=\"font-family: monospace\"> _________________________________________________________ <br>/  _____________________________________________________  \\<br>| | &lt;_&gt; &lt;_&gt; &lt;_&gt; &lt;_&gt; &lt;_&gt; &lt;_&gt;  |   |   |   |   |  &lt;_&gt; &lt;_&gt; | |<br>| |__|___|___|___|___|___|__&lt;_&gt;_&lt;_&gt;_&lt;_&gt;_&lt;_&gt;_&lt;_&gt;__|___|__| |<br>|  __________________________.__________________________  |<br>| |  |   |  &lt;_&gt; &lt;_&gt; &lt;_&gt; &lt;_&gt;  |  &lt;_&gt; &lt;_&gt; &lt;_&gt; &lt;_&gt;  |   |  | |<br>| | &lt;_&gt; &lt;_&gt;  |  &lt;_&gt; &lt;_&gt; &lt;_&gt; &lt;_&gt;  |  &lt;_&gt; &lt;_&gt; &lt;_&gt; &lt;_&gt; &lt;_&gt; | |<br>| | &lt;_&gt; &lt;_&gt; &lt;_&gt;  |  &lt;_&gt; &lt;_&gt; &lt;_&gt; &lt;_&gt;  |  &lt;_&gt; &lt;_&gt; &lt;_&gt; &lt;_&gt; | |<br>| | &lt;_&gt; &lt;_&gt; &lt;_&gt; &lt;_&gt;  |  &lt;_&gt; &lt;_&gt; &lt;_&gt; &lt;_&gt;  |  &lt;_&gt; &lt;_&gt; &lt;_&gt; | |<br>| |_&lt;_&gt;_&lt;_&gt;_&lt;_&gt;_&lt;_&gt;_&lt;_&gt;__|__&lt;_&gt;_&lt;_&gt;_&lt;_&gt;_&lt;_&gt;__|__&lt;_&gt;_&lt;_&gt;_| |<br>\\_________________________________________________________/</pre><pre style=\"font-family: monospace\"></pre><br>Now you try!<br><br>Abacus (soroban): https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Soroban<br>ASCII art credit: https://ascii.co.uk/art/abacus</span>\n</div>\n<div class=\"statement-section statement-protocol\">\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Input</div>\n      <div class=\"question-statement-input\"><strong>11 lines</strong>: A 59-character string, denoting a single row of the ASCII abacus.</div>\n   </div>\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Output</div>\n      <div class=\"question-statement-output\"><strong>Line 1</strong>: The value represented by the abacus in simplified form (with unnecessary leading/trailing zeroes removed). If the decimal value of the number is zero, <strong>omit the radix character (<const>.</const>)</strong> from the output as well.</div>\n   </div>\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Constraints</div>\n      <div class=\"question-statement-constraints\">The abacus frame will always be in the same position, as shown in the given examples.<br>Each vertical column (<const>|</const>) will always be in the same position, as shown in the given examples.<br>There are only 10 bead positions (denoting <const>0</const>-<const>9</const>), as shown in the given examples.<br>The middle row of the abacus frame will always have <strong>exactly one dot</strong> (<const>.</const>).</div>\n   </div>\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Example</div>\n      <div class=\"statement-inout\">\n         <div class=\"statement-inout-in\">\n            <div class=\"title\">Input</div>\n            <pre class=\"question-statement-example-in\"> _________________________________________________________ \n/  _____________________________________________________  \\\n| | &lt;_&gt; &lt;_&gt; &lt;_&gt; &lt;_&gt; &lt;_&gt; &lt;_&gt;  |   |   |   |   |  &lt;_&gt; &lt;_&gt; | |\n| |__|___|___|___|___|___|__&lt;_&gt;_&lt;_&gt;_&lt;_&gt;_&lt;_&gt;_&lt;_&gt;__|___|__| |\n|  __________________________.__________________________  |\n| |  |   |  &lt;_&gt; &lt;_&gt; &lt;_&gt; &lt;_&gt;  |  &lt;_&gt; &lt;_&gt; &lt;_&gt; &lt;_&gt;  |   |  | |\n| | &lt;_&gt; &lt;_&gt;  |  &lt;_&gt; &lt;_&gt; &lt;_&gt; &lt;_&gt;  |  &lt;_&gt; &lt;_&gt; &lt;_&gt; &lt;_&gt; &lt;_&gt; | |\n| | &lt;_&gt; &lt;_&gt; &lt;_&gt;  |  &lt;_&gt; &lt;_&gt; &lt;_&gt; &lt;_&gt;  |  &lt;_&gt; &lt;_&gt; &lt;_&gt; &lt;_&gt; | |\n| | &lt;_&gt; &lt;_&gt; &lt;_&gt; &lt;_&gt;  |  &lt;_&gt; &lt;_&gt; &lt;_&gt; &lt;_&gt;  |  &lt;_&gt; &lt;_&gt; &lt;_&gt; | |\n| |_&lt;_&gt;_&lt;_&gt;_&lt;_&gt;_&lt;_&gt;_&lt;_&gt;__|__&lt;_&gt;_&lt;_&gt;_&lt;_&gt;_&lt;_&gt;__|__&lt;_&gt;_&lt;_&gt;_| |\n\\_________________________________________________________/</pre>\n         </div>\n         <div class=\"statement-inout-out\">\n            <div class=\"title\">Output</div>\n            <pre class=\"question-statement-example-out\">12345.6789</pre>\n         </div>\n      </div>\n   </div>\n</div>"
